<title>NEW ZEALAND: BIL to break up LWR - newspaper.</title>
<headline>BIL to break up LWR - newspaper.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brierley Investments Ltd is preparing to break up clothing and textile manufacturer LWR Industries and sell off its companies, the Independent Business Weekly reported on Friday.  </p>
<p>The Independent said LWR's Canterbury International was likely to be sold overseas and that buyers had already been sought.</p>
<p>The paper said the break-up was the best way for BIL to profitably exit LWR, of which it owns 65 percent.</p>
<p>In June 1993, BIL floated 30 percent of the company, relisting it as LWR Industries.</p>
<p>The NZ$24 million offer -- 14.6 million shares at NZ$1.65 a share --- effectively valued the company at NZ$80 million.</p>
<p>Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
